WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.296 --> 00:00:02.600
- (Mark) So Wendy,

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.683
- (Wendy) Yes?

00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:07.669
(Wendy yawns, Wendy and Mark laugh)

00:00:07.669 --> 00:00:08.710
- (Mark) Where are you from originally?

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.467
- North Carolina, Charlotte.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.938
- (Mark) And how long
have you been out here?

00:00:11.938 --> 00:00:13.247
- (Wendy) 17 and a half years.

00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:15.285
- (Mark) 17 and a half years.

00:00:15.285 --> 00:00:17.743
And what, what got you out here?

00:00:17.743 --> 00:00:20.400
- My ex-husband, he beat me up.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.614
Well, I had a six week old baby that died.

00:00:23.614 --> 00:00:26.492
- (Mark) You had a six week
old baby that died? Of what?

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.633
- (Wendy) Her lungs gave out.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.576
- (Mark) Six weeks?

00:00:31.576 --> 00:00:34.244
- (Wendy) Six weeks.

00:00:34.244 --> 00:00:35.514
- (Mark) Was that your only child?

00:00:35.514 --> 00:00:40.216
- (Wendy) Oh, my first
child, my last child.

00:00:40.216 --> 00:00:44.262
And two weeks after I buried
her, I caught my best friend

00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:49.220
and my husband in our bed making love.

00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:55.115
Yeah, and I lost my mind.

00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:59.493
You know, I just buried my baby, our baby.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.594
And this is how you repay me?

00:01:02.594 --> 00:01:05.104
I pictured the life of our child.

00:01:05.104 --> 00:01:08.820
Don't spare him a thought,
he isn't worth it.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.820
So he shook this knife on
me, he wanted to cut me.

00:01:14.535 --> 00:01:15.766
- (Mark) Your husband?

00:01:15.766 --> 00:01:18.740
- (Wendy) Yeah. So this
fucking, ain't nobody will.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:23.956
I smiled and said, "get
out, you and her and both

00:01:23.956 --> 00:01:28.493
out my face" going was this,
just get out, leave me alone.

00:01:28.493 --> 00:01:31.583
And he's a stalker.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.060
He likes to stalk.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.950
So a friend of mine told me

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.469
California is a nice place to start over.

00:01:39.469 --> 00:01:44.420
So the battered women's
shelters down there got in touch

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.900
with me, got place down here and

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.360
they bought me a bus
ticket to come down here.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.223
Well, I get here and I lose
my luggage. Everything.

00:01:55.193 --> 00:01:58.500
Everything my son had, and everything.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.050
And like two months I called
the police department.

00:02:02.064 --> 00:02:04.410
They'll take you down
there, I'll call the police.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.791
I called the police and
this is where they bring me.

00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:07.641
Down to skid row.

00:02:11.738 --> 00:02:14.003
- (Mark) And you've been here ever since.

00:02:16.729 --> 00:02:19.130
Tell me about your childhood.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.410
You grew up, with one parent?

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.670
- (Wendy) My grandmother raised me.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.979
- (Mark) Your grandmother?

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:26.134
- (Wendy) When she died.

00:02:26.134 --> 00:02:27.467
I was eight.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.331
She died when I was eight.

00:02:30.331 --> 00:02:35.331
My father came back into the
picture and he was abusive.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.450
My grandmother passed away.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.713
My father beat me,

00:02:44.713 --> 00:02:48.633
for a whole month telling me
I killed her, it was my fault.

00:02:48.633 --> 00:02:51.400
It was my fault, my fault.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.660
So that's like eight year old.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.757
So, so I believing stuff like that.

00:02:55.757 --> 00:02:58.198
My grandma was my world.

00:02:58.198 --> 00:03:02.520
She was my only thing I had
this whole world taking care

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.845
of me, protected me, loved me and

00:03:04.845 --> 00:03:06.773
it killed me when she died.

00:03:08.307 --> 00:03:09.140
God, I love her.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.220
She had cancer.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.297
That's why I have it.

00:03:14.297 --> 00:03:16.456
- (Mark) You have, what kind of cancer?

00:03:16.456 --> 00:03:18.130
- (Wendy) I have stomach cancer.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.087
That's what I'm dying of.

00:03:20.087 --> 00:03:22.523
That's why I only have six months left.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.381
- (Mark) You also have AIDS?

00:03:28.381 --> 00:03:30.043
- (Wendy) HIV? Yeah.

00:03:34.092 --> 00:03:38.083
- (Mark) What drugs are you doing?

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:40.091
- (Wendy) Crack.

00:03:40.091 --> 00:03:41.812
- (Mark) You been doing
crack the whole time?

00:03:41.812 --> 00:03:44.532
- (Wendy) Yeah. Oh,
that's all that appears.

00:03:44.532 --> 00:03:47.063
I don't stick no needles and none of that.

00:03:47.063 --> 00:03:48.980
I came to the hospital.

00:03:50.957 --> 00:03:53.321
- (Mark) You have family?

00:03:53.321 --> 00:03:54.154
- (Wendy) None.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.242
- (Mark) So just you?

00:03:57.242 --> 00:03:59.973
- (Wendy) Just me.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.910
- (Mark) So after your
grandmother passed away,

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.253
you stayed with your..?

00:04:03.253 --> 00:04:04.304
- (Wendy) Father.

00:04:04.304 --> 00:04:06.283
And he was abusive.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:12.140
He raped me, it was so... I
don't want to talk about it.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.130
It was so terrible.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:18.440
He used to take belt buckles
and beat me in the face

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.273
with them.

00:04:23.466 --> 00:04:26.433
All these scars, they're from my father.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.660
Well, some of them are from here but,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.193
he slammed me and shot
me in the ass with a gun,

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.205
just to see if it felt good.

00:04:39.205 --> 00:04:40.255
- (Mark) He shot you?

00:04:41.695 --> 00:04:43.295
- (Wendy) I'd show you the Mark.

00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:48.127
It's like a mole, at the back of my ass.

00:04:49.051 --> 00:04:52.597
And he didn't ask me how that
feel, my father was sick.

00:04:58.563 --> 00:04:59.463
- (Mark) Your mom?

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:02.956
- (Wendy) My mom, I met her at one time.

00:05:02.956 --> 00:05:07.574
- (Mark) And why was your
mom not with you as a child?

00:05:07.574 --> 00:05:09.573
- (Wendy) 'Cause she didn't want me

00:05:09.573 --> 00:05:12.554
- (Mark) Was she an addict?

00:05:12.554 --> 00:05:15.621
- (Wendy) I don't know
Mark, nobody ever explained

00:05:15.621 --> 00:05:16.954
to me that part.

00:05:17.823 --> 00:05:20.363
All I know is she didn't want no baby.

00:05:21.813 --> 00:05:24.277
But I have three half
brothers that she had.

00:05:37.292 --> 00:05:38.125
- (Mark) But do you, I mean, your

00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:40.410
your view of the world must be affected

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.713
by what you've been through
or still going through.

00:05:43.713 --> 00:05:47.810
How do you view the world,
is it a horrible place?

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.263
Or do you see hope or?

00:05:50.269 --> 00:05:54.336
- (Wendy) I, I see hope now,
even though I have six months

00:05:54.336 --> 00:05:57.233
left, least I'm inside now.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.763
I got a little kitten on the way.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:05.707
I can't wait, gonna name her Penny.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:09.883
Little girl.

00:06:14.213 --> 00:06:17.863
She about like this, no, I'll
need real hunting for this

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.644
but I got it right there.

00:06:25.644 --> 00:06:26.477
- (Mark) What do you do for money?

00:06:27.556 --> 00:06:28.410
- (Wendy) I get care.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:33.410
I get that nine days per sec
or eight, eight days or so.

00:06:36.476 --> 00:06:39.874
- (Mark) Great, Wendy thank
you for talking to me.

00:06:39.874 --> 00:06:41.167
- (Wendy) Thank you, Mark.

